Z||000000||AusFiero||06-01-2001||09:36 AM||||Ok I have been toying with this for a fair while. How about bringing back the Fiero.<BR>Or maybe a rebody, a bloody expensive one taking the full glass roof with hidden framework into consideration. No I am not going to build it. Ask Pontiac.<P>Any ideas what should power and drive it? I have my own but am interested to see what people would use  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroconcept001.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||6
Z||000001||Raydar||06-01-2001||09:45 AM||||You never cease to amaze! That looks great!<BR>I would suggest a Northstar or LS1, or a 3800SC for a GTP version or Formula S. <BR>Have a regular 3800 for the GT and Formula.<BR>SE would get the 3400. Maybe a commuter model with the 4 cyl twin cam.<P>Was trying to think of an exotic drivetrain setup, but WTH!? I think the current four speed automatic should do nicely, with a 5 or 6 speed manual as an alternative.<P>That's a lot of different options/models, but we're dreaming. Right?  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 06-01-2001).]||||reg||14
