Z||000016||Tryxalon||06-02-2001||09:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>Ok I have been toying with this for a fair while. How about bringing back the Fiero.<BR>Or maybe a rebody, a bloody expensive one taking the full glass roof with hidden framework into consideration. No I am not going to build it. Ask Pontiac.<P>Any ideas what should power and drive it?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieroconcept001.jpg">  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yep. The possibility for this vehicle is a 3 rotor version of the HX-01. A Wankel running on Hydrozene and connected via a Continually variable Torodial transmission to a 30 KVA electric generator that powers the 4-wheel, computer controlled proportional power system. Of course, transversely mounted amidships for that low moment of polar momentum we love so much. <P>With Carbon fiber technology in the chassis and MPSRE engine control the power to weight ratio should be somewhere in the 4-7 lbs @ horse ratio. Distilled water as "fuel" cracked by onboard "by demand" hydrozene electro-catalyst on engine demand. <P><BR>And the only "pollution" is water vapor and the fast-food remains the driver tosses. ||||reg||6
